# Why a data warehouse exists

## Operational systems answer "now"

- Tuned for **tiny, constant reads & writes** — one order, one customer, one account
- Heavy analytical scans **slow the business down**
- Data sits **siloed** across many separate systems

## The warehouse answers "over time"

- A **central store** that collects from every source system
- Cleaned & organized **once**, with **history kept**
- Built for **reading & analysis** (OLAP) — fast, and never touches production
